From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Bug 2001075 - [Wayland] Report a drag ended by
 WaylandDragWorkaround as cancelled

WaylandDragWorkaround() ends the drag session with EndDragSession(true, 0)
on a session that never went through SourceEndDragSession(), so the dragend
event carries the session defaults: dropEffect "none", not user cancelled,
end point (0,0). The tab strip's handle_dragend() takes "no drop, not
cancelled" as a drop outside any target and checks the position; in a
maximized Wayland window event.screenX equals window.screenX, the strict
comparison fails, and the tab is detached into a new window.

The workaround fires on the release of a quick click on a tab, because the
release is already queued for the toplevel when gtk_drag_begin() grabs the
pointer and reaches button_release_event_cb() before any drag-motion. It
also fires when the compositor never finishes the drag (mutter issue 740),
the case it was written for. Nothing was dropped in either case, so mark
the session as user cancelled before ending it; handle_dragend() then
returns early on mozUserCancelled.

Origin: upstream, https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/commit/7dd748c3a7bf
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-13
---
 widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp b/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
index b9f7e3cf24134..e45d51344563f 100644
--- a/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
+++ b/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
@@ -217,6 +217,12 @@ void nsWindowWayland::WaylandDragWorkaround(GdkEventButton* aEvent) {
   NS_WARNING(
       "Quit unfinished Wayland Drag and Drop operation. Buggy Wayland "
       "compositor?");
+
+  // Nothing was dropped anywhere, so report the drag as cancelled. Without
+  // this the dragend event carries the session defaults (dropEffect "none",
+  // not cancelled, end point 0,0), which the tab strip reads as "dropped
+  // outside the window" and detaches the tab (bug 2001075).
+  currentDragSession->UserCancelled();
   currentDragSession->EndDragSession(true, 0);
 }
 
